.TH STEREO-MODEL-VIEWER 1 "2026-11-18" "Sparky Stereo OS"
.SH NAME
stereo-model-viewer \- open a 3D model, look at it and turn it
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B stereo-model-viewer
[\fIFILE\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
A Kirigami window with libf3d's 3D area inside it. Meshes, point clouds, splats and CAD files are read by the libraries of F3D.
On a stereo display the area is a surface of its own that Stereo KWin shows once for each eye; how far apart the two pictures are is
the depth the person set for the desktop (Display Settings), never an option of the program. With no depth limits from the
desktop the scene is shown flat and the program says so. The program's 3D options are Enable 3D, the render resolution of one eye
and a shortcut to Display Settings. The file is never written.
.SH SEE ALSO
f3d(1)
